## commit.push

Whether `vc-x1 commit` pushes what it commits in the same invocation, as `vc-x1 push` would after
it. True is the default, every commit published as soon as it is made: `--local` keeps one commit on
the machine, `--opening`'s bookmark included, and `--push` pushes one when the key is false. A commit with `--no-advance` pushes only with
`--push`, since its bookmark was left where it was. Owned by the work side because the commits are
the work repo's.

```toml
[commit.push]
homes = ["workspace-code"]
kind = "bool"
doc = "Default for commit: push what it commits, `--local` / `--push` override"
used-by = "vc-x1 commit --push / --local"
default = true
```

